00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:07.440
Now, speaking of monitoring well variability,

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:09.960
here's something I wish someone had told me

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:10.980
early in my career.

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:13.800
You arrive at a former service station

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:16.720
to resample after the phase two flagged benzene

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:20.300
above CSR schedule six standards in one well

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:23.120
but not the adjacent one eight meters up gradient.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:25.300
The difference is not random.

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:28.220
Vertical hydraulic gradients and subtle layering

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:31.360
in the fill unit often rooted dissolved phase mass

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:35.180
along preferential pathways that standard two inch wells

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:38.980
with 1.5 meter screens can miss or average out.

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:44.700
BCCSR protocol four and Ontario O-reg 153-04

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:48.720
both require documentation of screen placement

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:52.300
relative to the water table and any observed stratification.

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:55.940
Experienced assessors log the exact elevation

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:58.360
of the pump intake and compare it against

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:01.000
previous low flow stabilization data

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.760
rather than assuming uniform aquifer conditions.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:07.180
The insight that separates seasoned practitioners

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:09.980
is recognizing that a single non-detect

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:12.280
does not disprove plume extent

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:15.800
when the well screen straddles a low permeability lens.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:18.860
The most common mistake is immediately declaring

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:20.720
the plume delineated or reduced.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:24.020
The fixes to install a short screened well

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:26.920
or use a multilevel sampler at the same location

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:29.220
before adjusting the conceptual site model

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:31.220
or risk assessment assumptions.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:34.340
If you're working on groundwater monitoring

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:36.300
in British Columbia or Ontario,

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:41.020
review current Q2 sampling protocols against CCME

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:43.200
and provincial low flow guidance

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.820
to confirm intake placement documentation.

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:48.700
Update internal templates to capture

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:52.020
vertical gradient measurements on every monitoring event,

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:56.020
brief project managers on the need for multilevel confirmation

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:58.960
when nested wells show inconsistent results.

